s a 1-morphism <MATH_0007>\nwith <MATH_0008>, and\n<STRUCT_0005> any category fibred in sets <MATH_0009> is equal to <MATH_0010>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nIn particular, defining <MATH_0011> by the\nrule <MATH_0012>, we have\n<MATH_0013>\nMore precisely, given any map <MATH_0014> there exists a\n<MATH_0015>-morphism <MATH_0016> which induces\n<MATH_0017> on isomorphism classes of objects and\nwhich is unique up to unique <MATH_0018>-isomorphism.\n<STRUCT_0007>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:978fe8fd9eed68bff94bda7abc8856482d75eb1778f46e35d0e377e99c069e89", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:04SC:lemma/0001"}, "state": "BLOCKED"}, "reference:categories-lemma-2-category-fibred-sets": {"context_hash": "sha256:8e1562336c04152f86a546f2d90eeb11e6e05a688415d579617aa42ce24fc220", "kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 289070, "byte_start": 288192, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:56ffecd616d4f9f463decab016de174eafc896fdb970ce085b3ae43a5bc00b83", "line_end": 8088, "line_start": 8059}, "owner_tag": "02Y2", "parent_tag": "0042", "requested_label": "categories-lemma-2-category-fibred-sets", "requested_tag": "02Y2", "semantic_path": "lemma/0001", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0042", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{lemma-2-category-fibred-sets}", "LOCKED_0002": "\\begin{slogan}\nCategories fibred in sets are precisely presheaves.\n\\end{slogan}", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$2$", "MATH_0003": "$2$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\left\\{\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\text{the category of presheaves}\\\\\n\\text{of sets over }\\mathcal{C}\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right\\}\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\left\\{\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\text{the category of categories}\\\\\n\\text{fibred in sets over }\\mathcal{C}\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right\\}\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$F \\to \\mathcal{S}_F$", "MATH_0006": "$p : \\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\mapsto \\Ob(\\mathcal{S}_U)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-presheaf}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{lemma}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{lemma}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:66ec4e06012867a957280a05184fe6022e26ddf2e93d7fab80b969c56361e865", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4dedf7524bb10b3d2cb489857f123284401452157f626fae63ffc259e2110e91", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\n<LOCKED_0002>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a category.\nThe only <MATH_0002>-morphisms between categories fibred in sets are identities.\nIn other words, the <MATH_0003>-category of categories fibred in sets is a category.\nMoreover, there is an equivalence of categories\n<MATH_0004>\nThe functor from left to right is the construction\n<MATH_0005> discussed in\nExample <REF_0001>.\nThe functor from right to left assigns to <MATH_0006>\nthe presheaf of objects <MATH_0007>.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a178ac86fb5b00c3deda07c3aac33a5e51a15b8d56d82d7d8c8da434dcd7cc8d", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:02Y2:lemma/0001"}, "state": "BLOCKED"}}, "model_output": {"hash": "sha256:38af9591147e6fb1425a731aa9fa09f5b54247e3be0838c2bce34e1fd863cd82", "path": "docs/evidence/categories-completion-p017-raw.jsonl", "record_hash": "sha256:12fa3c7b8dac89f1e2dc570f291e4a57d24ff4e1bb99048285e28b1c12a100c7"}, "neighbor_unit_ids": [], "policy_revision": "git:e7a1627e7bce13592b8c07d43974a815ba27c0d5", "prompt_version": "translator-v2", "read_context": {"citations": [], "neighbors": [{"context_id": "inventory:categories:0045:proof/0001", "relation": "before"}, {"context_id": "inventory:categories:04SC:lemma/0001", "relation": "after"}], "references": [{"context_id": "reference:categories-lemma-2-category-fibred-sets", "label": "lemma-2-category-fibred-sets"}], "unit_id": "tag:04S9:prose-0004"}, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "s